<title>USA: GKN settles SEC probe, pays penalty.</title>
<headline>GKN settles SEC probe, pays penalty.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>GKN Holding Corp said on Wednesday that its primary operating subsidiary, GKN Securities Corp, has settled a U.S. Securities and Exchange Commisssion investigation.</p>
<p>GKN said that it paid a penalty of $100,000 and that Robert Gladstone, executive vice president of GKN, paid a penalty of $50,000.</p>
<p>According to GKN, the investigation arose out of consumer complaints against 10 brokers and alleged related supervisory failures during 1991 and 1992.</p>
